  "description": "Global Photovoltaic Power Potential by Country is a dataset listed in energydata.info, an open data portal for energy in developing countries under the section \"Solar\", published or maintained by World Bank Group. This dataset contains the GIS data used in the report, \"Global Photovoltaic Power Potential by Country\" generated by Solargis ( with funding provided by the Energy Sector Management Assistance Program (ESMAP). The study summarizes global solar resource and PV power potential on a country and regional basis. Coverage: 214 countries. It has 2 files in ZIP, XLS. The portal files it under Solar. The portal gives 2020 as the release date. It is reached through the links recorded on this page, with the catalogue entry as the discovery route. Access is free of charge and open. The licence is CC-BY-4.0. Caveats: this record was written from the catalogue listing only, so the linked page was not opened, its contents and current availability were not checked, and the description may lag the source. It can support power-system and electrification planning studies. Related record: the catalogue-level record data-energydata-info-world-bank.",
